;---------------------------------------
; BEGIN DECOMPILED SCRIPT
;---------------------------------------
<SCENARIO VER="105">
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{PLAYSND "togisuma.ogg" "BGM" "REPEAT" "1000" "0"}
{CREATECG "000" "グラフィック\背景\裏\警察署オフィス.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "C" "B" "0" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{CREATECG "文字カウント画像" "グラフィック\システム\文字カウント画像.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "C" "B" "0" "1" "0" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
<TXSPN>"Yaaawn..."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"</STYLE>Assistant Inspector Ise<STYLE ID="1">, you look sleepy. It is late, after all."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"Huh?
{PAUSE ""}
　Ah... not sleepy so much as... 
{PAUSE ""}
bored."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Well, there's nothing to do. We've finished the paperwork, and the materials for the next regular meeting too."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"Us being bored is a good thing, though. 
{PAUSE ""}
What happened this Golden Week?"<PG>
<STYLE ID="1">"Let's see... Leaving out traffic violations... </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">Two lost children, two shopliftings... </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">Two juveniles picked up for late-night wandering... </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">And then, let's see..."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"Haah... that's enough. That's about it, huh... 
{PAUSE ""}
In Minakami City they apparently had at least 10 burglaries of homes empty for the holidays..."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"This Motoki-cho really is peaceful, isn't it."</STYLE><PG>
"............ 
{PAUSE ""}
Hey, something's been bugging me for a long time..."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Yes?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"Don't you think it's strange?"
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Strange how?"</STYLE><PG>
"Motoki-cho's population is growing. In 2035 it's projected to hit 150,000. Nearly 4 times what it is now."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Well, that's true."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"Twenty years ago it was a fraction of today's population. 
{PAUSE ""}
And yet the crime rate per capita, even counting minor offenses, hasn't changed much. 
{PAUSE ""}
Well, the recent flayed-body case being the exception."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Um, so in other words, what..."</STYLE><PG>
"Motoki-cho's population growing means more people moving in from all over Japan."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Uh-huh..."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"And yet crime hasn't increased much. Any way you look at it, that's odd, isn't it?
{PAUSE ""}
　You could force the interpretation that the people who've always lived in Motoki-cho are good through and through, but the crime rate doesn't rise even as people move in from elsewhere. 
{PAUSE ""}
More than half of today's Motoki-cho is people who moved here from elsewhere, you know?"
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Now that you mention it... </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">Do you have any idea what's causing it?"</STYLE><PG>
"............ 
{PAUSE ""}
Ever since the flayed-body case, that sort of thing has started to bug me."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"............"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"Take this as my delusion and hear me out. 
{PAUSE ""}
Don't you think someone is forcibly turning Motoki-cho into a peaceful town?"
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Someone...?"</STYLE><PG>
"Yeah. For example... 
{PAUSE ""}
Yes, a drug that makes you feel constantly happy drifting in the air. 
{PAUSE ""}
So anyone who comes to Motoki-cho is drawn in and moves here."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Well... </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">As delusions go, I think it's interesting. There really are brain chemicals like that. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">But do you have a reason for a delusion like that?"</STYLE><PG>
"............ 
{PAUSE ""}
The truth is... 
{PAUSE ""}
Yeah... 
{PAUSE ""}
Promise me you won't tell anyone. If this gets around, it'll get messy. I'll take responsibility for you too."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"U-understood."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
{STOPSND "BGM" "3000" "PASS"}
"Look at this."<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CREATECG "アイテム1" "グラフィック\立ち絵\アイテム\注射器.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "650" "C" "100" "1" "1000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
<STYLE ID="1">"A syringe...?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
{PLAYSND "in_dream.ogg" "BGM" "REPEAT" "1000" "0"}
"Actually, I found this inside <STYLE ID="2">Mifuyu Niimura</STYLE>'s car."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"What!?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"A syringe with pink liquid in it. And there's a needle on it too. 
{PAUSE ""}
It's probably meant for use on the human body."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Uh-huh..."</STYLE><PG>
"What was <STYLE ID="2">Mifuyu Niimura</STYLE> planning to use this for...?"
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"There's no knowing that unless we ask </STYLE><STYLE ID="2">her</STYLE><STYLE ID="1">..."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"What if this is what made the spiriting-away-style method possible?"
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"No way...!"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"And look at this. A copy of something that was in the records room."<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{PLAYSND "SE\紙ペラ.ogg" "VOICE" "NORMAL" "1000" "0"}
{CREATECG "111" "グラフィック\背景\肉付き\検死結果2.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "R" "B" "200" "1" "1000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
<STYLE ID="1">"Additional information on </STYLE><STYLE ID="3">Eiichiro Niimura</STYLE><STYLE ID="1">'s death certificate..."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"When <STYLE ID="3">he</STYLE> died, his body was examined. 
{PAUSE ""}
It says that at the time, what looked like a drug and fragments of an organism were found. 
{PAUSE ""}
But on orders from the National Police Agency, that investigation was forcibly halted. 
{PAUSE ""}
So if this pink drug is connected..."<PG>
<STYLE ID="1">"</STYLE>Assistant Inspector<STYLE ID="1">... </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">that's no delusion...!"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"............ 
{PAUSE ""}
You think so...? I can't tell that either. 
{PAUSE ""}
They say no such drug was detected in <STYLE ID="2">Mifuyu Niimura</STYLE>'s body, though..."<PG>
<STYLE ID="1">"Which means there's a possibility this drug is in the bodies of </STYLE><STYLE ID="4">Ryoji</STYLE><STYLE ID="1"> and </STYLE><STYLE ID="5">Akane Kogori</STYLE><STYLE ID="1">, the perpetrators of the Megasawa City case...!"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"Yeah, I certainly can't deny it. 
{PAUSE ""}
But if there had been a positive result, I doubt that information would ever have come around to us. 
{PAUSE ""}
And as it says there, what was found in <STYLE ID="3">Eiichiro Niimura</STYLE>'s body was a drug similar to ephedrine."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Ephedrine...?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">"Roughly speaking, it's like a stimulant."</STYLE><PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{PLAYSND "SE\紙ペラ.ogg" "VOICE" "NORMAL" "1000" "0"}
{DELETECG "111" "1" "500" "0" "0" "" "0"}
{MESON "500"}
<STYLE ID="1">"Um, so to sum up... </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">This ephedrine-like stimulant is some kind of incredible doping drug, and it made the Megasawa City case possible. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">The people connected to that doping drug gathered in Motoki-cho. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">And this strangely peaceful Motoki-cho is connected to that doping drug...?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
{STOPSND "BGM" "3000" "PASS"}
"And also, yesterday I found an interesting website. This is a printout."<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{PLAYSND "SE\紙ペラ.ogg" "VOICE" "NORMAL" "1000" "0"}
{CREATECG "111" "グラフィック\背景\プリズン\雑誌.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "C" "B" "200" "1" "1000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
<STYLE ID="1">"Occult Magazine M?</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">　Ah, I know it, it's the one that runs obviously fake occult stuff and UFOs, right?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"Right. According to this article, long ago an organization was founded in Motoki-cho to study the goshinboku."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Huh, is that made up too?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"No, the organization itself apparently really existed. 
{PAUSE ""}
And not long after it was founded, every researcher in it was killed. 
{PAUSE ""}
There are investigation records from the time on this, so there's no doubt it's true."<PG>
{PLAYSND "日没廃校.ogg" "BGM" "REPEAT" "1000" "0"}
<STYLE ID="1">"A case like that? I never knew at all..."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"I only learned about it yesterday myself. Apparently the researchers were all beaten to death in their lodging."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Lodging...?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"Yeah, a lodging was built just to study the goshinboku. 
{PAUSE ""}
That's strange too. For the sake of one tree, a facility on that scale was built, you know?"<PG>
<STYLE ID="1">"Which means... </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">whoever set up that organization... um, I don't know if it was a sponsor or a public agency, but they must have considered the goshinboku extremely important, right?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"Right. In other words, I think that by this point, what the goshinboku really was had already been figured out to some degree."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"I see, and so, to study it in more detail..."</STYLE><PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{PLAYSND "SE\紙ペラ.ogg" "VOICE" "NORMAL" "1000" "0"}
{DELETECG "111" "1" "500" "0" "0" "" "0"}
{MESON "500"}
"And I found another interesting story. 
{PAUSE ""}
Apparently cherry pollen contains ephedrine."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Ephedrine, as in the one from before...!"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"Only, cherry pollen containing ephedrine is apparently a flat-out hoax. 
{PAUSE ""}
There's no scientific basis for it containing any such thing."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Hmm... But it all connects, to a creepy degree, doesn't it."</STYLE><PG>
"Yeah, even that hoax must have had some story it was based on. 
{PAUSE ""}
Suppose that was the goshinboku."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Um, so you mean the goshinboku's pollen contains ephedrine?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"If so, don't you think it would connect to why Motoki-cho has such an oddly low crime rate?"<PG>
<STYLE ID="1">"The pollen coming from the goshinboku is like a narcotic, and it makes people feel happy. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">So the crime rate is low, and people who've been to Motoki-cho can't forget how good it felt and move here... </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
Assistant Inspector<STYLE ID="1">, it's all connecting!"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"So what about in practice?
{PAUSE ""}
　When you leave Motoki-cho in spring, do you ever lose your sense of well-being, or feel some odd craving?"
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"No... I can't say I've ever noticed anything like that..."</STYLE><PG>
"Same here. Well, you and I were both born in Motoki-cho. 
{PAUSE ""}
Maybe if you live in Motoki-cho long enough, you build a tolerance to the drug and stop feeling anything. 
{PAUSE ""}
With narcotics, if you keep using, small doses stop working and the effect wears off sooner."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Then in the goshinboku cherry's case, it's giving off a narcotic that isn't addictive?"</STYLE><PG>
"Yeah. By the time the tolerance sets in, you've already built your whole life in Motoki-cho."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Hmm... But that theory contradicts itself, doesn't it?</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">　Then the happy feeling would go away too, so I don't think it connects to the low crime rate..."</STYLE><PG>
<BR>
"No, you can't say that for certain. 
{PAUSE ""}
A rise in crime along with the population growth was a concern we'd anticipated. 
{PAUSE ""}
That's why we've been calling on the schools and neighborhood associations to step up crime prevention. 
{PAUSE ""}
And a low crime rate means we police have our hands free more often, so it's easier to respond to minor incidents. 
{PAUSE ""}
To prevent big crimes, you start with small things. That's basic criminal psychology."<PG>
<STYLE ID="1">"That's broken windows, the broken windows theory, wasn't it?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"Yeah. If a broken window in a building is left alone, crime becomes more likely around it. 
{PAUSE ""}
That's because people see it as a place with few eyes watching. 
{PAUSE ""}
In Motoki-cho, where crime was low to begin with, it's easier to deal with small things like that."<PG>
<STYLE ID="1">"I see... So it does hold together, more or less."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"Well, it's only my delusion, nothing more. What if the goshinboku's pollen were a drug like that, is all."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Then, getting back to it, was that case where the researchers were beaten to death ever solved?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"No, in the end the culprit was never caught. It seems this case was hushed up by some kind of pressure too."<PG>
<STYLE ID="1">"Seriously... So every case or accident involving the goshinboku goes like that?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"That's right. After that beating-death case, the goshinboku research was promptly halted too."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"I'm starting to get scared of living in Motoki-cho... </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">Halting investigations into cases and accidents, that alone is plenty fishy, isn't it? </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">Could it be one of those government conspiracies?"</STYLE><PG>
"No, probably the opposite. They're hushing things up for people's safety. 
{PAUSE ""}
And this drug. Suppose it makes the spiriting-away-style crimes possible: what happens if that goes public?"
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Ah... It'd be the worst doping drug in history."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"I don't know how strong the effect is, but if it's beyond imagining, and something that terrifying got passed around on the black market, the balance of the world would go haywire."<PG>
<STYLE ID="1">"So the researchers were killed by someone who feared that?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"That's strange too. 
{PAUSE ""}
If that were the case, the killer would be someone who knew the goshinboku well. 
{PAUSE ""}
Well, it's unlikely an ordinary citizen did it. Which means someone in a public agency. 
{PAUSE ""}
If so, even without killing anyone, they could have just refused permission for the research from the start, or forced it to stop."<PG>
<STYLE ID="1">"I see... So that's why we can't tell who the killer really is..."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"And another thing... 
{PAUSE ""}
Have you ever hit someone with a mace?"
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Huh!? Of course not!"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"Beating a person to death is apparently harder than you'd think. You have to aim right at the head and bring a blunt weapon down hard. 
{PAUSE ""}
In the researcher killings, every single one was killed, without fail. 
{PAUSE ""}
It might be hard to picture, but it's not a method you'd easily imagine a human using."<PG>
<STYLE ID="1">"But I think it's worth looking into, don't you? This syringe is physical evidence to begin with."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"How would we look into it? Even if we send it for testing, won't it just get hushed up, like with <STYLE ID="3">Eiichiro Niimura</STYLE>?"<PG>
<STYLE ID="1">"Then, maybe have some university test it on the quiet..."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"That's no easy thing either. 
{PAUSE ""}
If it turns out to be something dangerous, it could become a big deal. 
{PAUSE ""}
Even the National Police Agency judged the <STYLE ID="3">Eiichiro Niimura</STYLE> matter would be bad if it went public, didn't it?"<PG>
<STYLE ID="1">"But... </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">then there's nothing we can do..."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"There's one way. Just one."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Really?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
{STOPSND "BGM" "0" "PASS"}
"I'll try using this myself."<PG>
{PLAYSND "最後の声・真呪殺\z50逆.ogg" "BGM" "REPEAT" "1000" "0"}
<STYLE ID="1">"W-wait a second! What if it's a deadly poison!?</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">　And if it turns out to be a stimulant, never mind getting fired, you'd go to prison!?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"What this chemical is remains unknown. 
{PAUSE ""}
As long as it isn't recognized as a stimulant or a narcotic, I won't be arrested."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"No, no, it's still dangerous!"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"............"<PG>
<STYLE ID="1">"Let's not do this. Turn this in to the National Police Agency. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">Then if the National Police Agency hushes it up, it means </STYLE>your<STYLE ID="1"> delusion was right. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">Isn't that enough..."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"............"
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Hey..."</STYLE><PG>
"Heh..."
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
{STOPSND "BGM" "3000" "PASS"}
"Hahahaha! Don't take it seriously!
{PAUSE ""}
　As if I'd use something this incomprehensible! Hahaha!"<PG>
<STYLE ID="1">"Wha, you're joking in this mood!?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"Sorry, sorry. But still, it's one sure-fire method, isn't it?"
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"It is, but please drop the stupid ideas!?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
"I know, I know."<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{PLAYSND "SE\携帯バイブ.ogg" "VOICE" "REPEAT" "1000" "0"}
{WAIT "3000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
"Hm? Who could that be at this hour?"
{WAIT "100" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{DELETECG "文字カウント画像" "1" "0" "0" "0" "" "0"}
<PG>
{STOPSND "VOICE" "3000" "PASS"}
<PG>
{}
<EVENT VALUE="MESEND">
